THOUGHT: NullAway flags formBuilder as @Nullable in addFormField. The method relies on the comment “Only called when isFormEncoded was true,” but NullAway doesn’t track that invariant. A safe, minimal fix is to add an explicit null check that throws an AssertionError if violated, which both preserves behavior (this should never be null here) and satisfies NullAway. I’ll update addFormField accordingly and then run the build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/retrofit && sed -i '205,215s/@SuppressWarnings("ConstantConditions") // Only called when isFormEncoded was true\./@SuppressWarnings("ConstantConditions") // Only called when isFormEncoded was true.
  void addFormField(String name, String value, boolean encoded) {
    if (formBuilder == null) {
      throw new AssertionError("FormBody.Builder must not be null when adding form fields.");
    }
    if (encoded) {
      formBuilder.addEncoded(name, value);
    } else {
      formBuilder.add(name, value);
    }
  }

  @SuppressWarnings("ConstantConditions") // Only called when isMultipart was true./' retrofit/src/main/java/retrofit2/RequestBuilder.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

